post.description:
Financial Rating of creditworthiness is calculated on the basis of following indicators:
•cash liquidity ratio which shows  amount of the most liquid short-term assets of the company to cover current liabilities;
•quick ratio which measures the ability of the company to use its near cash or quick assets to extinguish or retire its current liabilities provided timely settlements with debtors;
•current ratio which shows readiness to pay off its short-term liabilities;
•equity to current assets ratio which indicate the level of financial independence of the company;
•operating profit margin showing effectiveness of company's main activities.
